Package: kitverse
Title: Install and Load the KIT Research Tools in One Step
Version: 0.5.2
Date: 2026-11-02
Authors@R: person("Jie-Wen", "Tsai", email = "tsai.jiewen@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: One package that installs the KIT research tools and everything
    they need: 'kits' (item calibration, linking and scoring), the 'shiny'
    apps 'kitsUI' and 'kitJoin', and the shared interface package
    'kitDesign'. It checks the computer (R version, package library, package
    versions, and whether each app really starts) and updates packages that
    are missing or too old. Like 'tidyverse', library(kitverse) attaches the
    core packages and lists their versions and conflicts; the apps are then
    started with their own run_kitsui() and run_kitjoin(). Loading the
    'kitverse' namespace loads none of the other packages, so the check and
    the update still work when a package is broken.
